      "includes_after": {
        "allegro.h": [
          "winalleg.h"
        ]
      },
      "evidence": "DWARF of main.c declares LARGE_INTEGER (play local `li`) and calls LoadLibraryA, QueryPerformanceCounter, QueryPerformanceFrequency, ShellExecuteA and WSAStartup; the original call sites use the stdcall symbols (_LoadLibraryA@4). Allegro's documented way to reach the Win32 API is <winalleg.h> after <allegro.h>, which provides these declarations, WSADATA and MAKEWORD/LOBYTE/HIBYTE. The hand-written stdcall prototypes and the WSADATA/MAKEWORD copies in main.c are substitutes for that header; LoadLibraryA was implicitly declared and relied on the linker's stdcall fixup.",
      "removed_text": [
        {
          "name": "ShellExecuteA",
          "text": "extern void *__attribute__((stdcall)) ShellExecuteA(void *hwnd,\n    const char *operation, const char *file, const char *parameters,\n    const char *directory, int show);\n"
        },
        {
          "name": "WSADATA",
          "text": "typedef struct {\n    unsigned short wVersion;\n    unsigned short wHighVersion;\n    char szDescription[257];\n    char szSystemStatus[129];\n    unsigned short iMaxSockets;\n    unsigned short iMaxUdpDg;\n    char *lpVendorInfo;\n} WSADATA;\n"
        },
        {
          "name": "WSAStartup",
          "text": "extern int __attribute__((stdcall)) WSAStartup(unsigned short version,\n                                                WSADATA *data);\n"
        },
        {
          "name": "MAKEWORD",
          "text": "#define MAKEWORD(a,b) ((unsigned short)(((unsigned char)(a)) | \\\n                    ((unsigned short)((unsigned char)(b)) << 8)))\n"
        },
        {
          "name": "LOBYTE",
          "text": "#define LOBYTE(value) ((unsigned char)((value) & 0xff))\n"
        },
        {
          "name": "HIBYTE",
          "text": "#define HIBYTE(value) ((unsigned char)(((value) >> 8) & 0xff))\n"
        }
      ]
    },
